  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(168, 35, 143)\n\n(182, 65, 127)\n\n**Logic:** **Second no. = [(First no. - Third no.) + 10]**\n\n**(168, 35, 143) →**\n\n⇒ [(168 - 143) + 10]\n\n⇒ (25 + 10) = 35\n\n**(182, 65, 127) →**\n\n⇒ [(182 - 127) + 10]\n\n⇒ (55 + 10) = 65\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. (142, 83, 69)**\n\n⇒ [(142 - 69) + 10]\n\n⇒ (73 + 10) = **83 = Second Number**\n\n2. (253, 99, 154)\n\n⇒ [(253 - 154) + 10]\n\n⇒ (99 + 10) = 109\n\n3. (203, 89, 117)\n\n⇒ [(203 - 117) + 10]\n\n⇒ (86 + 10) = 96\n\n4. (159, 62, 87)\n\n⇒ [(159 - 87) + 10]\n\n⇒ (72 + 10) = 82\n\nHere, **(142, 83, 69)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (1)\".",
